From: Christian Ehrhardt <christian.ehrhardt@codasip.com>
Subject: Update linux kernel headers to our UAPI and fix compile

The iptables sources come with their own version of the linux
kernel headers, presumably because iptables needs newer versions
than those available on various build environments.

This is not a problem with our setup so just copy all linux
kernel headers that shipped with the iptables tarball from
our linux-libc-headers package.

This results in minor compile errors. Fix those.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ CHERI specific ]

